  - '#atelier-studio'
  - '#studio'
symbols_created:
  - '#compute-letterbox-fit'
  - '#canvas-size-presets'
decisions:
  - id: TD-2026-05-28-llm-mutation-on-existing-source
    decision: Server emits llm:mutation envelope after ?source=existing compose-success; browser WS filter loosened from hardcoded project.atelier to ${activeProjectName}/${currentDocPath}
    rationale: Envelope-driven refresh is the studio's established pattern; alternative (browser explicit reload) would create two refresh paths. Filter loosening also fixes a latent flat-docs-pivot bug affecting any MCP tool mutation against non-project.atelier docs.
  - id: TD-2026-05-28-canvas-letterbox-fit
    decision: Canvas letterbox-fits the available container area via computeLetterboxFit + ResizeObserver; native pixel dimensions stay at doc.canvas.width/height; only CSS sizing scales
    rationale: Preserves raster fidelity for export while letting any aspect ratio (portrait/landscape/square) fit the available area without overflow. ResizeObserver handles panel reflow + window resize. observe(this.el) not parentElement to avoid feedback loop.
  - id: TD-2026-05-28-canvas-size-presets-v1
    decision: v1.0 ships 4 closed presets (1080×1920, 1920×1080, 1080×1080, 1080×1350); Custom… is v1.1; existing captions show inline warning but resize is not blocked
    rationale: Smallest viable surface that covers 95% of social-content aspect ratios. Custom is a dialog with bounds validation (v1.1). Auto-recompose captions on resize would require transcript + clip metadata at toolbar layer (much larger refactor) — warn-but-allow keeps the affordance usable for empty-or-track-only docs (the common case).
